<p>A randomized controlled feeding trial by Ebbeling and colleagues (2022) compared diets varying in carbohydrate content and found favorable changes in insulin-resistant dyslipidemia markers among participants on the lower-carbohydrate diet. This supports a mechanistic link between carbohydrate restriction and improved insulin sensitivity.</p>
